      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are correct that the real-world evidence often suggests that the systemic, global \"spillover\" costs outweigh the benefits to targeted domestic sectors. This fragmentation often results in higher inflation and less competitive national industries in the long run. While political arguments favor immediate, targeted wins, the consensus in most advanced economic analysis is that extreme protectionism ultimately acts as a brake on overall global and national prosperity.",
